{
  "uid": "urnetwork-extender-camouflage",
  "title": "urnetwork / extender camouflage",
  "tags": [
    "urnetwork",
    "extenders"
  ],
  "description": "What clients' and extenders' tcp camouflage came to across the fleet, from their reports (connect/EXTENDER-SPLICE-ROLLOUT.md, Reporting path; controller/extender_camouflage_report.go): the numbers the rollout gates of EXTENDER-UPDATE2 §3 are judged against. Off by default on both sides, so this is empty until a cohort reports. Every failure on the path undercounts and none overcounts, and clients that cannot reach the api are not here. Internal only.",
  "editable": false,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timezone": "",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "env",
        "label": "env",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "warp-mimir"
        },
        "query": "label_values(urnetwork_extender_camouflage_reports_total, env)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "reports",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "reports by how they ended (per hour)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "warp-mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "warp-mimir"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (increase(urnetwork_extender_camouflage_reports_total{env=\"$env\"}[1h]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Every report the api answered at POST /network/extender-camouflage-report: accepted, counted; accepted_extender_ignored, counted without its extender part, since the caller has no active extender; duplicate, a retry of a report already counted, which added nothing; rate_limited, past the client's 12 an hour; disabled, reports are off (camouflage_report.enabled in extender.yml, the kill switch); too_large, malformed and out_of_bounds, refused for what it holds; unavailable, Redis or the fleet read could not answer. Nothing but rate_limited and unavailable is posted again. No reports at all means no cohort is on: the sender is off unless its space sets ExtenderGatedPreference, or connectctl extender runs with --camouflage_report."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "reports not counted (per hour)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "warp-mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "warp-mimir"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (increase(urnetwork_extender_camouflage_reports_total{env=\"$env\",outcome!~\"accepted|accepted_extender_ignored|duplicate\"}[1h]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The reports that added nothing and were not a retry of one that did. Each of these is a report the numbers below do not hold, so read a rise here before reading a change below. A sender stays inside every bound, so too_large, malformed and out_of_bounds that persist are not senders that behave. accepted_extender_ignored on the panel to the left that does not fall is clients claiming to be extenders; their extender part is dropped."
    },
