          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (increase(urnetwork_extender_camouflage_client_outcomes_total{env=\"$env\"}[1h]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "From clients' reports, one line per counter of connect.ExtenderTcpCamouflageClientStats: camouflage_won, legacy_won (the Phase A fallback), both_failed (the Phase B loss a skewed or legacy-fronted client meets), refused, camouflage_unauthenticated (Phase A terminate), camouflage_leaf_rejected (Phase B splice), and the reasons a dial ran legacy alone, legacy_only_no_key, legacy_only_fingerprint, legacy_only_no_front_name. A client's counts are its own word: one identity can add at most 65,536 per counter per report and 12 reports an hour, so a line that jumps alone is worth checking against the reports panel before it moves a gate."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
